# fastboot-m install hook

post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
fastboot-m: use `fastboot-m` (short name), or `fastboot-meowarch` — both are
  symlinks to the same binary. The distro's android-tools `fastboot` is left
  untouched, so both can be installed side by side.
  USB works like platform-tools; if `fastboot-m devices` is empty but lsusb
  sees the phone, install udev rules (AUR: android-udev) or run as root.
  mke2fs/make_f2fs/mke2fs.conf live in /usr/lib/fastboot-m/ and are found
  automatically by the fastboot binary (same-directory lookup).
EOF
}